               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 89-year-old male patient. He presented with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, raising clinical suspicion for appendicitis. Clinical examination revealed peritoneal irritation at McBurney's point. Blood tests demonstrated leukocytosis consistent with an acute inflammatory process. Abdominal ultrasound confirmed appendiceal inflammation. Given the confirmed diagnosis of acute appendicitis, the patient was taken to theatre and underwent a laparoscopic appendectomy without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, he received intravenous fluid replacement, analgesic medication, and prophylactic antibiotics. Wound care was provided and recovery was satisfactory. The patient was mobilised with physiotherapy support and discharged home in stable condition on postoperative day five. Please ensure appropriate follow-up and wound review. Do not hesitate to contact me should any concerns arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
